1. Remote Site Setting
 A security whitelist in Salesforce that allows Apex to make HTTP callouts to an external endpoint.❗It does NOT store authentication details
Purpose
    Allow outbound callouts to an external URL
    Prevent unauthorized data exfiltration
Key Characteristics
    Only stores protocol + domain
    Required for Apex callouts (unless using Named Credentials)
    No credential management
    Hardcoded auth headers needed in Apex    

Add into - Remote Site URL: https://api.example.com
Example
    HttpRequest req = new HttpRequest();
    req.setEndpoint('https://api.example.com/data');
    req.setHeader('Authorization', 'Bearer ' + token);
    req.setMethod('GET');
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Named Credential
A secure Salesforce abstraction that stores:
        Endpoint URL
        Authentication details
        Automatically injects auth headers
Purpose
    Simplify callouts
    Secure credential storage
    Remove hardcoded secrets from Apex
Key Characteristics
    Supports multiple auth types
    Automatically handles tokens
    No Remote Site Setting required
    Endpoint referenced dynamically
Supported Authentication
    No Auth
    Basic Auth
    OAuth 2.0
    AWS Signature
    JWT Bearer Flow
Example
    HttpRequest req = new HttpRequest();
    req.setEndpoint('callout:My_Named_Credential/data');
    req.setMethod('GET');

    ✅ No authorization header
    ✅ No token handling
    ✅ More secure

Side‑by‑Side Comparison (Interview Gold)
    | Feature            | Remote Site Setting     | Named Credential                 |
    | ------------------ | ----------------------- | -----------------------------    |
    | Purpose            | Allow external callouts | Allow + authenticate callouts    |
    | Stores credentials | ❌ No                    | ✅ Yes                         |
    | Security           | Low                     | High                             |
    | Token handling     | Manual                  | Automatic                        | 
    | Retry / refresh    | ❌ No                    | ✅ OAuth refresh supported     |
    | Hardcoded secrets  | ✅ Yes                   | ❌ No                          |
    | Admin friendly     | ❌                       | ✅                             |
    | Best practice      | ❌ Legacy                | ✅ Recommended                 |
    ***
